---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Corrections & Suggestions" description="Report a correction or propose a Korean heritage field-guide topic through Dama Korea’s public GitHub issue tracker." noindex={true}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell visual-shell"><div><p class="eyebrow">Corrections desk</p><h1>Help keep the field notes accurate.</h1><p class="page-hero__lede">Reports use a public GitHub tracker so the issue, replies and status remain visible. Never post personal or sensitive information.</p></div></div></section>
  <article class="legal-shell article-body">
    <div class="contact-action"><strong>Open a public report</strong><a class="button" href={SITE.correctionsUrl} rel="external">Create a correction or guide suggestion</a></div>
    <h2>For a correction</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Include the Dama Korea page URL.</li><li>Identify the sentence, visual, caption or instruction in question.</li><li>Explain what changed and when you observed it.</li><li>Include the responsible organization’s current page when available.</li></ul>
    <h2>For a guide suggestion</h2><p>Describe the place or practical problem, who encounters it and what existing English-language resources fail to make clear. Dama Korea prioritizes topics that fit the heritage field-guide mission and can be verified responsibly.</p>
    <h2>How the channel works</h2><p>A GitHub account is required to open an issue. The issue, replies and status are public. Dama Korea does not provide a private email address, private contact form, booking service or urgent travel support.</p>
    <h2>Privacy</h2><p>Do not post passport details, reservation codes, faces, private addresses, financial information or unpublished personal correspondence. If a matter cannot be described safely in public, do not submit it through this channel.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
